WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.001
With Sweden poised to

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:03.536
become the 32nd member of NATO's

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.304
president, Biden

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.505
avoided what could have been

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.573
a serious headache

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.208
throughout the NATO's summit.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:08.975
A short time ago,

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.910
I spoke with a Swedish prime minister

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.978
about Ukraine's

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.013
desperate push

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.181
to follow in Sweden's footsteps.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.950
And in this CNN exclusive,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.084
he shed some light on

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.052
President Biden's role

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.354
in clearing the path for Sweden to join

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.092
We have felt a very, very strong

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.528
support and commitment from the

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.630
United States and from President Biden

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.731
all the time.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.967
And very explicitly

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.136
illustrated by the invitation

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.570
to the White House last week.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.606
So we really feel a strong support

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:43.576
from from major NATO's allies,

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.211
including, of course,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.048
our neighboring countries.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.350
So all the details between

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.185
between other countries, I cannot

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.486
really tell we have had.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.288
We have had

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.589
good negotiations

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.793
between Sweden and Turkey and

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.995
and the NATO's system itself

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.229
on fighting terrorism.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.765
That has been the main the main

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.202
question for our for our discussions

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.305
Prime Minister, you mentioned

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.440
seeking protection

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.941
as one of the main goals

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.443
in your rejoining the alliance.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.377
We've repeatedly

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.578
heard tough talk

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.314
from the Kremlin about Sweden and Finland

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:22.916
joining NATO's.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.249
And today,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.018
Dmitry Peskov, a spokesperson

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:25.952
for the Kremlin,

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.121
said that there would be countermeasures.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.623
Do you read that as a threat

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.393
What is your level of concern

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.596
Well, we are

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.666
quite used to those threats

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.934
and the kind of threats

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.671
they have been repeated by the Russians

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.039
all the time

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.007
against Sweden and against Finland.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.175
So that is nothing new.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.510
But of course,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.379
we are concerned by it, by a decision

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:56.883
from Asia and by other ways of trying to

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.085
to engage

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.653
in an illegitimate way

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.956
into the Swedish politics, of course.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.290
But I think we are

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.893
we are strong people are almost immune,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.196
immune against that kind of propaganda.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.032
So I think we will handle this as well.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:13.366
And

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.468
not least since

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.469
the scene

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.205
since Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.574
Everybody in the world, including Russia,

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.276
they know where we stand.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.012
They know that we are on Ukraine's side

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.213
in this war.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.282
We help Ukraine in different ways.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.451
So so becoming a NATO

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.020
ally is a very natural step as well.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.089
You'll get translation.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.790
What should NATO's approach

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.093
then be to ending the war?

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.728
Do you believe that the West needs

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.863
to offer Vladimir Putin an off ramp

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.765
toward a cease fire?

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.104
Well, I don't have any

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.472
any other view

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.240
than most other countries right now

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.743
where we stand on Ukraine's side.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.444
The Ukraine

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.281
must win on their terms.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:04.350
The war must end and Ukraine's future

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.720
must lie in the hands of the Ukrainians.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.056
All these are fundamental principles.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.892
That also is the reason why we always

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.994
repeat the fact that

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.930
Ukraine is not only fighting.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.565
It's the war for itself.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:21.301
It's also fighting the war for all other

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.671
European and other democracies

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.006
that want to to

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.442
to decide the future by themselves.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.843
So I think this is an

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.412
extremely important task.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.446
And we will

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.081
we will do what it takes to

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.183
to to continue our help to Ukraine.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:42.222
On that note, winning on Ukraine's terms,

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:43.856
at least publicly from President

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.225
Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.927
has meant retaking Crimea.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.295
And military experts say

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.196
that that would require

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.931
a level of investment

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.433
in Ukrainian forces

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.035
that to this point has not been made.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.370
Are you,

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.538
as part of NATO's, now

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.439
prepared to make

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.007
those significant investments?

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:01.941
And does it worry you

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.443
that it could lead to a further

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.978
escalation with Russia

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.416
Well, very many NATO

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.252
countries are providing

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.187
Ukraine with different kinds

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:15.922
of material weapons,

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.290
including Sweden, of course.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.825
And that was also a historic decision

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:21.227
in Sweden to to start doing so.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.296
But we have done it in a in a pretty

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.432
impressive way, if I may say myself,

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.935
and we continue to do that. So.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:31.604
So I think that's the right way of

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:32.872
doing it.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.107
Of course, the Ukrainians,

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.409
they they realize they need even more

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:39.145
and they are very precise in what they

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.114
and what they wish.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.249
And I think we have done

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.217
our share of that.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.052
And we continue to do our share of that.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:46.619
But of

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.454
obviously different countries

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.522
or all countries

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.057
have to make their own decisions on that.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:54.060
But I need to some if we feel

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.462
a very strong support for for Ukraine

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.031
for very natural reasons,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.467
So not

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.402
long ago, Jens

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.770
Stoltenberg said that

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.139
NATO's would invite Ukraine

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.807
to join the alliance

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.842
when conditions are met.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.879
What are those conditions

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.050
Well, I have to be honest,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.285
Sweden, we are not yet

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.422
a full member of NATO's.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.357
So I will not go into

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.726
I won't as a nonmember so far.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.061
I will not have any

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:31.531
any views on how NATO's an organization

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.800
should should act

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.903
in relation to another country

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.438
which is not a need to members.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:40.373
I think that that is a

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:43.476
that is a reasonable and necessary

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.347
principle for me right now.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.181
We support

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.249
Ukraine and benefited different ways

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.150
and we do it together

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.985
with other countries as well.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.755
But we don't have any views on

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.924
how need the right now should

00:05:57.924 --> 00:06:00.159
act in relation to Ukraine.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:02.362
Well, there

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:02.929
are significant

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.030
concerns from the White House,

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.998
for example, about domestic corruption

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:06.933
within Ukraine.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.968
And national security spokesperson

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.104
John Kirby told CNN this morning

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:12.739
that Ukraine would need to work

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:13.606
on those issues

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.541
in order to be part of the alliance

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.643
that you will soon join.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.846
Do you have concerns about corruption

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.947
in Ukraine?

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:24.417
Well,

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.386
as I said, on and on, the relation

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.020
between need two in Ukraine,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:28.755
Sweden do not

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:29.188
and does

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.991
not have any any any opinions of our own

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.326
What I can

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:33.826
say, though,

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.762
is that since we've had

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.796
the same discussion

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:40.767
on Ukraine's cooperation on accession to

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.402
to the European Union,

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:43.136
I've been following

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.670
that extremely closely,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.673
being the Swedish presidency.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.176
And regarding that,

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:52.578
there were set up some criteria for

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:56.082
for Ukraine to to make progress

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:59.886
within to be able to to start

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:02.688
the negotiations.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:03.756
And that

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.791
will be a full report

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:06.526
during fall

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:07.126
this year

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:09.595
on how these criterias are developing.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:10.830
And I think most countries

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.831
and in the European

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.667
Union are very impressed by the ability

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:17.703
from the Ukrainians to to

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:20.039
to deliver results

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.474
on these areas

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:23.609
in spite of an ongoing war.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:24.844
So basically,

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:26.179
I do believe in Ukraine,

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:26.913
but I will stick

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.748
to not having any opinions on

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:29.449
how NATO's

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.851
should act in regards to Ukraine.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:36.088
Our thanks to Swedish Prime Minister Ulf

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.056
Kristersson for taking the time

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.392
during that busy day of NATO's diplomacy.

